  "releaseNotes": "0.4.2: Fixes wrong positions for Chiron, Pholus, Ceres, Pallas, Juno and Vesta. Their heliocentric file records were returned without adding the barycentric Sun, shifting geocentric longitudes by up to ~0.11° (Ceres) and ~0.03° (Chiron). Asteroid positions now match the Swiss Ephemeris C library to sub-milliarcsecond level and are covered by golden tests.",
